            <profile id="4863-0670-63f0-41c5" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon. May ride a horse (+8 pts), a warhorse (+16 pts), and have light armour (+3 pts) or heavy armour (+4 pts), shield (+2 pts), short bow (+2 pts) or bow (+3 pts). Amirs may have thrusting spear (+2 pts). Mounted characters may have half-barding (+2 pts) or barding (+4 pts) for their mounts. Characters leading units of infantry or dismounted cavalry may be Riding Horses (+2 pts) or Riding Camels (+2 pts). In Arab Conquest and Umayyad armies characters may not ride warhorses and may not take half-barding or barding for their mounts. Amir as Army General: if no Khalifa is chosen, an Amir may be upgraded to Army General (+25 pts). 0-2. Not available to Arab Conquest armies (their only general is a Companion upgraded to Army General). (Byzantium p.82)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="84b6-74a1-8bb7-316e" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
