            <profile id="1105-cae0-0870-eeda" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon. May ride a horse (+8 pts), a warhorse (+16 pts), and have light armour (+3 pts), heavy armour (+4 pts) and shield (+2 pts). The Army Standard Bearer may have half-barding (+2 pts) or barding (+4 pts). Standard Bearers leading units of dismounted cavalry may be Riding Horses (+2 pts) or Riding Camels (+2 pts). 0-1. (Byzantium p.82)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="968d-dcef-e27b-7a6b" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
