            </profile>
            <profile id="d26b-2db2-8a34-8e08" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, shield, light armour &amp; bow. May have heavy armour (+1 pt), and either thrusting spear (free) or Kontarion (+1 pt). Senior Ghulams may take 'Amud Maces (+1 pt, treat as Heavy Mace), and barding for their mounts (+4 pts). Dismounted Ghulams Option: may dismount (-12 pts, Movement 4), and may be Riding Horses (+1 pt). Mounted Ghulams are Superior Turkish Cavalry. Senior Ghulams must be led by the Army General at all times. 0-1 units. The senior Ghulams were the ruler's personal bodyguards, who all swore their allegiance to him. (Byzantium p.82)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="21bf-6f8e-4cff-1954" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="3+">
