  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="98f7-1627-ac5d-b633" name="Early Caliphates (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>EARLY CALIPHATES (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.76-84): armies of the Arab Conquest, the Umayyad and Abbasid Caliphates and their successors, 632-1073 AD. Special rules: Rivalry (documented only): if two or more rival ethnic groups are fielded, roll a D6 for each rival unit at the beginning of the first turn; on a 1 the unit remains stationary (it may reform, defend itself in close combat and shoot at chargers), repeated each turn. Combined Formations, Naffatun per-unit limits and "Infantry and Cavalry" combined percentages are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Early Caliphates - Arab Conquest]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Special Units: up to 0%
  ARAB CONQUEST ARMIES (632-660 AD). Characters up to 33% (Companions, Shaikhs and an Army Standard Bearer); Cavalry up to 33% (no Abbasiya Light Cavalry); Infantry at least 50% (Guards and Levies may not be chosen; four Mutatawwi'a units); Special Units none. The only general is a Companion upgraded to Army General (+25 pts). Characters may not ride warhorses, nor take half-barding or barding. City Militia Skirmishers may only take short bows. Formed Mutatawwi'a and Volunteers are subject to all the Warband Psychology rules (not just Rules 1 &amp; 2), and may be Stubborn (+2 pts). Volunteer Skirmishers have Leadership 7 (free) and may have throwing spear (+1 pt). Two units of Volunteer Skirmishers may be upgraded to Elephant Slayers (+2 pts per model).
[Early Caliphates - Umayyad Caliphate]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  UMAYYAD CALIPHATE (661-750 AD). Characters up to 25% (no Companions); no Ghulams; Cavalry up to 50% (no Abbasiya Light Cavalry); Infantry at least 33% (no Guards; two Mutatawwi'a units); Special Units: two units of Mountainmen. Characters may not ride warhorses, nor take half-barding or barding. Formed Mutatawwi'a and Volunteers are subject to all the Warband Psychology rules.
[Early Caliphates - Early Abbasid Caliphate]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ghulams: up to 40%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%
  Special Units: up to 33%
  EARLY ABBASID CALIPHATE (750-861 AD). Characters up to 25% (no Companions); Ghulams up to 40%; Cavalry up to 50%; Infantry up to 75% (one unit of Mutatawwi'a; if Ghulams have been chosen, no Guard units may be taken - not enforced); Special Units up to 33%. Special rules as the Later Abbasid Caliphate. From 813 AD, Ghulams gradually became the core of the standing army.
[Early Caliphates - Later Abbasid Caliphate]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ghulams: up to 66%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  Special Units: up to 33%
  LATER ABBASID CALIPHATE (861-1055 AD). Characters up to 25% (no Companions); Ghulams up to 66% (if Turkish Ghulams are chosen, at least two units of Turcoman Cavalry must be taken as well - not enforced); Cavalry up to 50% (no Abbasiya Light Cavalry); Infantry up to 33% (no Mutatawwi'a or Guards); Special Units up to 33%; two units of Hamdanid Heavy Cavalry may be chosen as well. Special rules: Abbasid armies led by an Army General may use the Stratagem special rule. In Abbasid armies, Regular Cavalry may be upgraded to Superior Arab Cavalry (+2 pts); such units may not take spears. Rivalry: if both Turks and Buyid Daylamites are fielded, they become subject to Rivalry (documented only).
[Early Caliphates - Aghlabids]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ghulams: up to 33%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  AGHLABIDS (800-909 AD). Characters up to 25% (Shaikhs, an Army Standard Bearer and an Amir); Ghulams up to 33% (Greek Heavy Cavalry and Italo-Lombard converts - from the Italo-Lombard list only mounted Milites, Stipendiarii and Pueri; Italo-Lombards are documented only); Infantry at least 33% (no Guards; two Mutatawwi'a units); Cavalry up to 33% (one unit of Abbasiya Light Cavalry); Special Units up to 25%, on Khurasan Cavalry only. City Militia troops may not use the Leadership value of the Army General. Aghlabid City Militia and Volunteer Infantry skirmishers have Feigned Flight.
[Early Caliphates - Tulunids &amp; Ikhshidids]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ghulams: up to 33%
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Infantry: up to 66%
  TULUNIDS &amp; IKHSHIDIDS (868-969 AD). Characters up to 25% (Shaikhs, an Army Standard Bearer and an Amir); Ghulams up to 33% (no Daylamites or Armenians); Infantry and Cavalry together up to 66% on troops described as Arab, Volunteers and City Militia (as 'Abids; the combined cap is applied to each category here); two units of Guards may be chosen; Special Units: only Naffatun. As the best 'Abid infantry, two units of Guards may be chosen. All other 'Abid units should be represented by using the City Militia profiles.
[Early Caliphates - Early Fatimid Caliphate]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ghulams: up to 33%
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Infantry: up to 66%
  EARLY FATIMID CALIPHATE (909-1073 AD). Characters up to 25% (no Companions); Ghulams up to 33%; Infantry and Cavalry together up to 66% on troops described as Arab, Volunteers and City Militia (as 'Abids; the combined cap is applied to each category here); two units of Guards may be chosen; Special Units: only Naffatun (up to two per City Militia skirmisher unit). Early Fatimid Heavy and Light Cavalry may not take thrusting spears. Rivalry: if any two or three of the Turkish, Daylami and North African 'Abid elements are fielded they become subject to Rivalry (documented only).
[Early Caliphates - Hamdanids]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Ghulams: up to 50%
  Cavalry: up to 75%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 33%
  HAMDANIDS (929-1004 AD). Characters up to 25% (an Amir, Shaikhs and an Army Standard Bearer); Ghulams up to 50%; Cavalry up to 75% (no Abbasiya Light Cavalry); Infantry at least 25% (no Guards; one unit of Mutatawwi'a); Special Units up to 33% (no Khurasan units). Hamdanid armies led by an Army General may use the Stratagem special rule. Hamdanid Heavy Cavalry cost 23 pts, have WS4 and count as Superior Arab Cavalry.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
